\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fs20\cf0 The main duty of ZipALot is to extract all ZIP files from one directory to another. To do this, s\plain\f1\fs20\cf0 imply enter the source directory that contains the ZIP files and the target directory where they shou\plain\f1\fs20\cf0 ld be extracted and hit the unzip button.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fs20\cf0 \{bmc UnzipButton.BMP\}\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fs20\cf0 To select a directory, simply hit the directory picker button. \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fs20\cf0 Every time you select a new source directory, the target directory is updated with the name of th\plain\f1\fs20\cf0 e source directory and a subdirectory called "unzipped". To prevent this update, you can lock the tar\plain\f1\fs20\cf0 get directory, by activating this checkbox.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fs20\cf0 Hit the "Filter settings" button to open the filter options.\par
