\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 A nice feature of ZipALot is the possibility to apply filters to your unzip action.\par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Hit the "Filter settings" button to open the setting dialog.\par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 \{bmc WholeWindow.bmp\}\par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs28\cf0\b What are filters?\par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 You probably never worked with Linux or DOS, eh? :-)\par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Filters are a way to filter (what else :-) out certain files. You can use \plain\f0\fs20\cf0\b wildcards \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 to specify yo\plain\f0\fs20\cf0 u filter-rule.\par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 The wildcards you can use are * and ?\par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 * matches any number (also null) of characters in the filename\par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 ? machtes exactly one character (including "no" character)\par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs22\cf0\b Some examples:\par
\keep\keep \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
{\pard\trowd\trgaph57\trleft0\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw0\cellx1629\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw0\cellx8480\intbl{\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 *.zip\cell}
\intbl{\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Get all files with the ending zip. * matches any name of any length.\cell}\row
\intbl{\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 m*.zip\cell}
\intbl{\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Get all the files that start with m and have the ending zip.\cell}\row
\intbl{\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 m*10.zip\cell}
\intbl{\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Matches the files that begin with an m, end with 10 and have the ending zip\cell}\row
\intbl{\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 mback?.zip\cell}
\intbl{\tx720 \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Finds mback1.zip, mback2.zip mbackX.zip, but not mback10.zip etc.\cell}\row
\intbl{\tx720 \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 mback??.zip\cell}
\intbl{\tx720 \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Finds mback1.zip, mback10.zip and mbackXY.zip etc.\cell}\row
\intbl{\tx720 \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 rg*.c??\cell}
\intbl{\tx720 \ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Finds rg1.c01, rglong.c20 etc.\cell}\row
}\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs28\cf0\b Filter\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs22\cf0\b ZIP-files Filter\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 This filter tells Sir ZipALot which archives in the source directory should be processed. Only ZI\plain\f0\fs20\cf0 P files that match the expression will be extracted.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 You only can enter ONE filter rule in this field.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs22\cf0\b Extract Filter:\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Only files which match this rule will be extracted from the ZIP files.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 You can add more than one rule! Separate them with a slash /\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 I.e. the rule "*.jpg/*.gif/*.png" would extract all jpeg, gif and png graphic files from the arch\plain\f0\fs20\cf0 ives.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs22\cf0\b Don't extract Filter:\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Files that match this expression won't be extracted from the ZIP files.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 You can also here add multiple rules by separating them with a slash /\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 I.e. the rule "*.avi/*.mpg/*.mpeg/*.mov" would not extract these movie files from the ZIP archives.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs22\cf0\b Case Insensitive filters\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 If this option is set to true, the filters will be case-insensitive. This means that the case of \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 the filenames that are stored in the ZIP files does not matter.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri240\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 The extract rule "m*.nfo" will extract "MYTH.NFO" and "my.nfo".\par
\page\page \ql\li0\fi0\ri240\sb0\sl\sa0 }
