\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 There are some other options that will be explained here:\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs30\cf0\b Overwrite files\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 Existing files in the target directory will be overwritten and replaced. ATTENTION! There is no w\plain\f0\fs20\cf0 ay to undo that. Once a file is overwritten it's lost!\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 If more than one ZIP files is extracted at the time and if some of the archives contain files wit\plain\f0\fs20\cf0 h the same name, only the last one will "survive". The others will be overwritten.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs30\cf0\b Extract only newer\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 If this option is set, only a file that is newer then a file with the same name in the target dir\plain\f0\fs20\cf0 ectory is extracted.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs30\cf0\b Recreate directories\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 If the archive contains directory information, you can decide if the directories shall be recreat\plain\f0\fs20\cf0 ed or not.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri510\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f0\fs20\cf0 After you made your settings, you can p\plain\f0\fs20\cf0\v Topic5>main\plain\f0\fs20\cf0 review the result.\par
\ql\li0\fi0\ri7095\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
